        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f3b65538-c521-5bf6-919e-caad27bba0d9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of Hürtgen Forest, Battle of Pusan Perimeter\n- People: John W. Minick\n- Organizations: United Nations, United States Army\n- Places: Hürtgen Forest, Western Front\n- Concepts: World War II, Medal of Honor\n\nFacts:\n- The Battle of Hürtgen Forest was a series of fierce battles fought from 19 September to 16 December 1944 between American and German forces on the Western Front during World War II in the Hürtgen Forest about 50 square miles east of the Belgian–German border.\n- John W. Minick was a United States Army soldier who received the Medal of Honor for his actions during the Battle of Hürtgen Forest in World War II.\n- The Battle of Pusan Perimeter was a large-scale battle between United Nations and North Korean forces that lasted from 4 August to 18 September 1950.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
